#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235302 :multistep/context "Consider the family of functions $f(x)=\\frac{x-2}{{x}^{2}+4x+k},$ where $k$ is a constant." :multistep/id #uuid "bfc4f516-9fb4-57dc-9dd1-2cd295ad420e" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235623 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235357}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235628 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235354}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235706 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235353}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235718 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235358}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235750 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235356}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235785 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235355}}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235303 :multistep/context "Consider the initial value problem \n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=x{y}^{2},\\,y(1)=2.\n$$" :multistep/id #uuid "c147697d-6e49-572d-8166-45a84bc192bc" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235624 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235349}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235641 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235350}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235655 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235351}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235731 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235346}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235736 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235352}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235744 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235347}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235775 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235348}}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235304 :multistep/context "![](images/ae/ae44c9f19c7afc26c399999105b7d17c6e2e6b3e020e7b419065a8514741dc9b.png)\n\n \n\nConsider a circle with radius $3$ centered at the point $(3,0),$ shown above." :multistep/id #uuid "c3a8aa31-cb9d-5828-a311-bd67392da03c" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235607 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235496}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235649 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235498}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235687 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235500}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235695 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235501}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235751 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235497}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235764 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235499}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235791 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235502}}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235305 :multistep/context "A particle $P$ is moving along a curve in an $xy$-plane such that the $x$-coordinate of $P$ is given by\n\n$$\nx(t)=\\frac{2t}{(2{t}^{2}+3)^{2}},\\,t>0\n$$\n\nwhere $x$ is the distance of $P$ from the origin, measured in meters, and $t$ is measured in seconds." :multistep/id #uuid "cbb272f1-f5dc-5a8e-a5ad-90bddee2754a" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235586 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235384}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235616 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235391}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235648 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235388}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235674 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235386}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235686 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235387}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235723 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235390}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235732 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235382}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235743 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235389}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235762 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235385}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235777 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235383}}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235306 :multistep/context "![](images/22/22a909d34b63517bf5ccf90560a8070d20e1aa91a6c9eaf8f4e5326208b9d751.png)\n\n \n\nThe shell above is obtained by rotating the curve $y=2{x}^{2}$ for $x\\in [0,1]$ by $2\\pi $ radians about the $x$-axis, as shown above. For each point $(x,y,z)$ on the shell, the charge density (electric charge per unit surface area) of the shell is given by the function \n\n$$\nd(x,y,z)=\\frac{x({y}^{2}+{z}^{2})}{\\sqrt{16{x}^{2}+1}}.\n$$" :multistep/id #uuid "d2f519ed-b682-5c5b-a212-a6f310187d1d" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235585 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235463}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235594 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235462}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235601 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235460}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235712 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235464}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235766 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235461}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235784 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235466}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235794 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235465}}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235307 :multistep/context "![](images/c1/c1d9f53c6aed4acd378f8554df5c8beaaea81e169b5284e51f87204a87b3d53d.png)\n\nA housing complex designed by an architect is shown in the coordinate plane as the region $R$ with vertices $ABCD.$ A highway lies on the line $l$ with equation $2x+y+1=0.$ The area of the complex is $16$ hectares." :multistep/id #uuid "e3d5311c-0e28-5039-bfac-4c86234f4171" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235633 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235397}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235658 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235396}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235661 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235393}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235663 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235392}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235666 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235394}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235782 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235395}}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235308 :multistep/context "![](images/f4/f437bd795c0ccf57a45299bd5f2ff2ac79c5f6bee599183cf7f7463c34fb3edb.png)\n\nThe thin rectangular plate shown above has the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=2x{y}^{2}.$" :multistep/id #uuid "e64b3651-363e-559b-8703-b33e695a40c5" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235588 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235556}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235614 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235553}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235644 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235549}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235678 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235555}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235711 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235552}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235715 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235554}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235717 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235551}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235719 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235550}}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235309 :multistep/context "![](images/f4/f47c5a0a1cc62bc6aca913adea9f496e1a666017ec1cf5610b01535bf497af0d.png)\n\n \n\nConsider the three-dimensional region of air shown above. All the surfaces of the region, except for the top one, are parallel to the corresponding coordinate planes. The velocity field of the airflow is defined by \n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)={z}^{2}\\,i+2xy\\,j+x{y}^{2}\\,k.\n$$" :multistep/id #uuid "ed4fde3a-03ae-5199-ad7c-856fd9a816b6" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235653 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235535}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235657 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235540}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235670 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235539}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235692 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235537}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235698 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235536}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235756 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235538}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235792 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235541}}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235310 :multistep/context "Let $T(t)$ represent the temperature of an object at time $t,$ in minutes, since the moment when it was put in a room. The temperature *decreases* at a rate that is equal to $0.03$ times the difference between the object's temperature and the room's temperature, which is ${25}^{∘}\\text{C}.$" :multistep/id #uuid "f0a99d46-ce15-56e3-b510-9d2f7d70f87e" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235592 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235518}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235620 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235519}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235645 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235517}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235707 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235521}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235749 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235520}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235758 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235516}}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235311 :multistep/context "The velocity, in $\\text{m/s}$, of a subatomic particle is modeled using the function $v(t)=2{csc}^{2}⁡(t)$ for $\\pi <t<2\\pi .$" :multistep/id #uuid "f1e50ebd-abae-5c45-863b-21e026e0e2dc" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235625 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235449}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235630 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235446}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235632 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235445}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235651 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235451}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235689 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235447}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235753 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235448}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235768 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235450}}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235312 :multistep/context "Consider the function $f$ defined by $f(x)=\\frac{7}{2{x}^{2}-5x-3}.$" :multistep/id #uuid "f3d1d1fe-b389-598e-8032-fa51aeb6ebae" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235583 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235367}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235631 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235369}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235685 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235368}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235694 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235371}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235709 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235372}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235734 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235370}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235742 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235373}}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235313 :multistep/context "Consider the following functions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(x)&=\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{x} \\\\\ng(x)&=8x-\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3} \\\\\nh(x)&=-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" :multistep/id #uuid "fa5e8226-be39-5b3e-bbe4-f074324839a2" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235608 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235430}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235626 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235435}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235646 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235432}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235726 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235436}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235739 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235429}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235760 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235431}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235765 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235434}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235781 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235433}}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235314 :multistep/context "An ambulance service helicopter takes off from a hospital helipad three times on a particular day. The helicopter's location a few seconds after these takeoffs are given by points $P,$ $Q,$ and $R.$" :multistep/id #uuid "fbc3fee1-e819-58be-962e-1b2abc135cb8" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235593 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235512}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235610 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235513}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235667 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235514}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235691 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235515}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235693 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235511}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235725 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235510}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235728 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235509}}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362462 :multistep/context "![](images/b8/b8b8e65b34ae0ae59f7cb291a49fd829cae58555b1fc1f267ac57fc70b63b323.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows an air duct whose surface $S$ encloses a region in the shape of a rectangular solid. A turbine draws air in through the top inlet and expels it through the bottom outlet. The flow of air through the duct is given by the vector field $G,$ where \n\n$$\nG=⟨0,0,-xy-2{z}^{2}⟩.\n$$" :multistep/id #uuid "2f3860dd-8198-51d7-b3a1-ee15d077253f" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362558 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362527}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362561 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362508}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362568 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362524}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362569 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362511}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362575 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362530}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362577 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362505}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362580 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362502}}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362463 :multistep/context "![](images/56/56260e9bf38aa5f93b95d76a2b9b63252003c4bf08d7225cd677684fb3eff833.png)\n\nA cylindrical meshed heater is submerged in a tub of water. The surface of the heater is described by the equation ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=9$ for $0\\le z\\le 3.$ The heater is open at the top and bottom and has heating elements at $z=1,2$ on its surface to increase the temperature of the water." :multistep/id #uuid "c14a6fb6-60ba-5c85-9e86-d97f2cade274" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362559 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362496}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362562 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362472}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362565 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362483}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362566 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362499}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362576 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362489}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362579 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362465}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362581 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362486}}]}]}
